-- title:
--   A point of a double cone is nonzero
-- statement:
--   If $h$ lies in the double cone $V(v,\vartheta)$ then $h \ne 0$.
--
--   A double cone in Bux–Kassmann–Schulze is the union of two opposite open half-cones, each
--   of which excludes its apex: membership is stated by an angle condition together with
--   $h \ne 0$, since the angle at the origin is undefined. This records the consequence in the
--   form the descent arguments of Section 5 use, where a chain of lattice points inside a cone
--   is ordered by distance to the tip and the tip itself must be excluded.
--
--   A supporting lemma, not a numbered result of the source.
